# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This guide walks you through using the GOV.UK Content API for the first time.
You'll retrieve GOV.UK content by making a GET request to the API, which returns
the content as JSON.

## Who this is for

You can use this guide if you are a developer or a non-developer who understands
the basics of [APIs][api-def].

## Before you start

Make sure you have one of the following tools:

- a terminal with a data transfer utility, such as [curl][curl]
- a dedicated API client such as the [Postman][postman-install] app

## Authentication

You do not need to authenticate or include any custom HTTP headers to use the
GOV.UK Content API.

## Base URL

The base URL for all requests to the GOV.UK Content API is:

```txt
https://www.gov.uk/api/content/
```

## Make your first API request

To make your first request to the GOV.UK Content API:

1. Choose a page on the GOV.UK website, for example [https://www.gov.uk/take-pet-abroad][take-pet-abroad].
1. Make a note of the URL component after the domain, which for our example is:
   `/take-pet-abroad`.
   This URL component is the **path** that you will send to the API.
1. Add this path to the end of the API's [base URL](#base-url).
1. Using your preferred tool, make a GET request to the resulting URL. For example,
   use the curl utility in the terminal:
   <pre><code class="language-shell">curl https://www.gov.uk/api/content/take-pet-abroad</code></pre>

You get a JSON response containing the GOV.UK content. The fields contained in
this response are explained in the [API reference][api-reference].

Alternatively, you can use the Postman app to make the GET request. Follow the
Postman [quick start][postman-quick-start] guide to do this, using the API URL
in your request in place of the example provided:

```text
https://www.gov.uk/api/content/take-pet-abroad
```

## Next steps

Now that you've made your first API request, you can:

- [learn how the GOV.UK Content API works][how-it-works]
- [retrieve and display GOV.UK content][retrieve-and-display]

